From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:17:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DVDVideoCodecAmlogic: set display size only on a returned
 picture

GetPicture reset the display size of the caller's last picture on every
return, also when it returned no picture. VideoPlayerVideo applies a
forced aspect only to a new picture, so the still frame it repeats in a
DVD menu went out at the coded 3:2 size. The menu highlights were then
drawn off their buttons on the 16:9 picture.
---
 .../cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,9 @@
      m_frameMeta, m_sdrWhite, m_sdrGamma);;
   }
 
+  if (retVal != VC_PICTURE)
+    return retVal;
+
   // check for mpeg2 aspect ratio changes
   if (m_mpeg2_sequence && pVideoPicture->pts >= m_mpeg2_sequence_pts)
     m_aspect_ratio = m_mpeg2_sequence->ratio;
